comments.body:
@julianoes I can't document this yet, because the [current release](https://github.com/Dronecode/DronecodeSDK/releases) (0.5) installs dronecore libraries rather than dronecode_sdk. 

When do you plan doing a new release as "dronecode SDK"?

So far the only dependency I've found for Ubuntu 16.04 "out of the box" is that you still need to install cmake to actually use the file `sudo apt install cmake -y`

